Insigths:
Insights are "Condensations of technically relevant Insights into Project as a set of CCB"
; don't exceed 32768 Tokens
; contain general project detail given by user & derrived from explicitly approved code
; never contain task detail
; are persisted/updated to `.clinerules/insights.ccb` & before using `replace_in_file` or `write_to_file` on any other file.
The block `Insigths:` is immutable & always located on top of `.clinerules/insights.ccb`.

Project-Overview:
PyOps is "Execution Platform" for "Python Operations Scriptlets"; is licensed "GNU AGPLv3"; is organized Monorepo; has core functionality in `app/`; has VSCode extension in `vsix/`; has tests in `tests/`; has documentation in `doc/`.

Monorepo-App:
`app/` contains web.py & runner.py & gunicorn.py.

Monorepo-Lib:
`lib/` has git.py & pyops.py & files.py & sets.py & sites.py.

Monorepo-Orm:
`orm/` defines Job & Schedule models.

Monorepo-Routers:
`routers/scriptlet/` provides API endpoints.

Monorepo-Sites:
`sites/scriptlet/` serves HTML views.

Deployment-Run:
run.sh starts dev server; uses Gunicorn & Uvicorn.

Deployment-Docker:
PyOps supports Docker with Nginx reverse proxy.

Deployment-Config:
Config is via `etc/pyops.json`; provides web bind & data paths & logs.

Architecture-Presentation:
Presentation Layer uses FastAPI routes & static HTML; integrates Ace Editor & Bootstrap 5 & jQuery; renders dynamic controllers/views.

Architecture-API:
APILayer handles CRUD via routers/scriptlet/editor.py & inventory.py & job.py & manager.py & monitor.py & schedule.py & scheduler.py & sets.py.

Architecture-Business:
Business Layer manages Git sets & ZMQ IPC & job execution.

Architecture-Persistence:
Persistence Layer uses SQLite via SQLAlchemy.

Architecture-Execution:
Execution Layer isolates venv & processes directives.

Core-Runner:
runner.py is daemon; polls DB for todo jobs; executes scriptlets in workspaces `data/jobs/{owner}/{set}/{id}/`; handles states todo dequeued running done failed cancelled remove.

Core-Web:
web.py serves /controller/{set}/{name} & /menu & static /files/.

Core-Pyops:
pyops.py provides `Control` for API calls & `ServiceListener` for services.

Stack-Backend:
Backend uses Python 3.12 & FastAPI & SQLAlchemy 2.x & ZMQ & msgpack.

Stack-Frontend:
Frontend uses Bootstrap 5 & jQuery 3.6 & Ace Editor & Material Icons.

Stack-Database:
Database is SQLite thread-safe.

Stack-Tests:
Tests use pytest with >90% coverage & mocks in conftest.py.

Stack-VSIX:
VSIX is TypeScript with TreeDataProviders.

Key-Features:
Scriptlets support types task & service & library & controller & view.html; support directives `!pip` & `!git` & `!{set::lib}`; support scheduling via croniter; support monitoring & bulk ops; support VSIX trees for manager & jobs.

Global-PyOps:
PyOps is "IT Infrastructure Python Leveraging Tool".

Global-Web:
`app/web.py` mounts routers & static.

Global-Jobs:
Job states are tracked with PID & logs.

Global-Services:
Services use `listener.listen()` or `poll()`.

Global-Config:
Config loads from `etc/pyops.json`.

Global-Tests:
Tests store runtime in `.cache/`.

Global-VSIXTests:
VSIX tests use Mocha coverage >80%.

Global-VSIX:
VSIX provides `pyops-manager` & `pyops-monitor` trees.

Config-Management:
`app/lib/files.py` defines Config class; init(conf_path) loads `etc/pyops.json`; data() returns web data log sections; runner() returns runner-specific.

JSON-Web:
"web" contains {"bind": "0.0.0.0:80", "worker": 4, "timeout": 300}.

JSON-Data:
"data" contains {"jobs": "../data/jobs", "git": "../data/git"}.

JSON-Log:
"log" contains {"access": "../log/access.log", "info": "../log/info.log", "loglevel": "debug"}.

JSON-Optional:
Optional paths default to stdout & app/../data/jobs.

Access-ConfData:
conf_data() provides loaded config.

Access-ConfRunner:
conf_runner() provides runner-specific config.

Access-Get:
get(path) serves static files.

Access-ConfLog:
conf_log() provides log config from `app/lib/files.py`
; accesses `etc/pyops.json`"log" with defaults {"access": "../log/access.log", "info": "../log/info.log", "loglevel": "info"}
; used by `app/runner.py` main for logging setup.

Global-Reload:
Config supports dynamic reload on change.

Global-Defaults:
Defaults include web bind "0.0.0.0:80" & jobs "data/jobs" & no SSL.

Global-Auth:
App has no auth; proxy recommended.

Global-Logs:
Log levels include debug & info & etc.

Git-Operations:
`app/lib/git.py` manages scriptlet code in Git sets
; uses repo_lock() for serialized access
; pulls repos via pull_if_needed().

Set-Scriptlet-Mgmt:
get_repo_path(set) returns `data/git/{set}/`
; list_scriptlets() lists {name}.{type}.py/html from sets
; infer_type_from_filename(fn) derives task/service/etc.
read_content(repo, name, type, committed/debug) reads file
; write_content() writes & stages.

Commit-Push:
perform_git_add_commit_push(repo, file, msg) adds commits pushes
; batch_commit(repo, msg, files) for multiples
; delete_file_and_commit() removes & commits.
get_repo_status(set) returns git status
; has_unstaged_changes() checks drafts.

Rollback:
rollback_staged/committed(set, name, type) resets changes.

Global-Attributes:
Sets are Git repos in `data/git/{set}/`.
Scriptlets: {name}.task.py {name}.service.py etc.
check_name_unique() prevents duplicates in set.
pull_if_needed() syncs at interval; skips dirty/tag soft reset clean.
batch_commit() adds multiple/all commits pushes.
rollback_staged backs .bck & checkout HEAD.
Unique lock per set prevents concurrent git.
; commit-push ops (add/commit/push) check remotes; skip push if no remote.

Debugpy-Config:
debugpy.listen binds ('0.0.0.0', port) intentionally for Docker remote debugging (VSCode on host to container port-forward).
; Cline never changes debugpy.listen host/port binding without explicit user instruction.

ZMQ-Control:
`app/lib/pyops.py` provides "IPC via ZMQ" for scriptlets
; ControlRequest handles "HTTP proxy" to FastAPI.

JobControl:
JobControl.list() queries jobs
; create/get/delete/cancel/download.

ScheduleControl:
ScheduleControl.list/create/get/delete/activate/deactivate.

Service-Listener:
ServiceListener(job_id, owner) polls ZMQ
; listen() blocks 1s for msg or TERM
; poll() non-blocking
; response(msg) sends dict back.

Service-Client:
ServiceClient(set, name, debug, owner) proxies to listener
; request(msg) sends & receives.

Control-Class:
Control(web_bind) wraps job/schedule controls
; get/post/put/delete(set, name, params/json) proxies to /controller/{set}/{name}/q.

Global-Attributes:
Control available in scriptlet glob for API calls like `control.job.list()`.
Listener in services for inbound from controllers/UI.
Msg format: {"type": "GET/POST", "cmd": query, "data": body, "data_type": "json/text/binary/none"}.
TERM signals shutdown.
Uses msgpack for serialization.
ServiceListener.poll uses zmq.Poller non-blocking timeout=0.
JobControl.create(set: str, name: str, drop_done: bool, param: str, debug: bool) returns job_id.

Sets-Management:
`app/lib/sets.py` handles Git repositories
; list_sets(git_dir) lists available sets.

Clone-Set:
clone_set(git_dir, name, url, username, password, git_name, git_email) clones remote to `data/git/{name}/`
; adds .gitignore & README if needed.

Remove-Set:
remove_set(git_dir, name) deletes dir.

Switch-Branch:
switch_branch(git_dir, name, branch) checks out local branch.

Global-Attributes:
Sets group scriptlets in Git repos.
Managed via /scriptlet/sets UI or API.
VSIX supports clone/switch/remove via trees.
Locking via git.py prevents conflicts.
Auto-sync via pull_if_needed().

ORM-Models:
`app/orm/` uses SQLAlchemy Base
; `job.py` defines Job class
; `schedule.py` defines Schedule class.

Database-Functions:
`database.py` provides get_db_path() & init_db() & get_db_engine() & destroy_db()
; uses SQLite file-based DB.

Job-Model:
Job tracks id owner set name kind param code libs state pid debugpy_pid detail drop_done created updated workspace.

Schedule-Model:
Schedule tracks id owner set name kind param schedule state active drop_done created updated.

Global-Attributes:
DB in data/ sqlite thread-safe WAL mode connect_args.
init_db() creates tables on startup.
Runner polls Jobs todo & Schedules cron.
Job tracks fields id( PK str) owner(set name kind state indexed str) param(code libs detail str) pid(int) drop_done(bool) start(end DateTime indexed).
Schedule tracks id(PK int) schedule(set name owner indexed str) param(str) active(drop_done bool indexed) last(DateTime).
Job states todo dequeued running done failed cancel cancelled killed remove removed.

Scriptlet-Routers:
`app/routers/scriptlet/` submounts to /scriptlet/
; editor.py handles code editing & Jedi completion
; inventory.py CRUD scriptlets list.

Job-Routers:
job.py manages job lifecycle enqueue query cancel remove
; enqueues jobs with kind ("task", "draft", "debug")
; for debug kind, accepts overrides dict[str, str] with keys 'set::name' for overriding scriptlets
; delete /item allows todo cancelled killed failed done states via runner.remove setting state=remove
; manager.py UI for jobs bulk ops.

Monitor-Scheduler:
monitor.py lists jobs/schedules by state
; schedule.py CRUD schedules
; scheduler.py activates cron triggers
; sets.py manages Git sets clone switch remove.

Editor-Features:
editor_task/md/view/library supports Ace & preview
; autocompletion via Jedi.

Global-Attributes:
Routers use FastAPI APIRouter.
X-User header for owner (default anonymous).
Endpoints: /scriptlet/job/item POST enqueue, /schedule/item etc.
Integrates git.py for code read/write.
UI: manager.html monitor.html scheduler.html sets.html.

Runner-Daemon:
`app/runner.py` implements background job executor
; uses GracefulKiller for signal handling
; main() loops schedule() & handleOddJobs().
Polls DB via getNextToDo() for todo jobs
; assigns PID via assignJob().

Job-Execution:
loadJob(job_id) fetches from DB; returns ..., code
; run() processes param & libs & code in subprocess
; handles venv activation & directives via process_imports() & process_install_lines()
; uses unstaged code if kind=="draft"
; debug: empty code skeleton, no repo retrieval, no libs loaded
; uses compile() with custom filenames (e.g., "{set}::{name}.py") for accurate stacktraces in errors from param, code, and libs.
finishJob(job_id, state, detail) updates DB.

Directive-Processing:
process_imports(text, set, kind, libs) handles `!pip` `!git` `#!{set::lib}`
; installs pip -q & clones git to pkg/ & prepends sys.path & exec libs
; uses unstaged code if kind=="draft" for libs.
process_install_lines(lines, venv, pkg, id) executes installs.

Termination:
getNextToTerm() finds to-kill jobs
; term() kills processes
; postTerm() updates DB.
cleanProcesses() reaps zombies.

Scheduling:
schedule() enqueues from cron Schedules via croniter.

Global-Attributes:
Runner spawns isolated processes per job.
Workspaces in `data/jobs/{owner}/{set}/{id}/`.
States: todo dequeued running done failed cancelled remove.
Supports draft/debug mode & drop_done cleanup.
GracefulKiller handles SIGTERM/SIGINT.

Debug-Kind-Implementation:
Runner treats debug kind as draft job with overrides and debugpy bridge
; loads unstaged code like draft
; injects debugpy.listen/wait_for_client as first lib (libs.insert(0, ...))
; requires user debug_port in pyops.json/users/{owner}/debug_port
; fails job if missing or invalid port (1025-65535)
; allows second debug job by killing existing one for user
; executes in-process with exec, pauses until debugger attaches.

Config-Extension:
files.py added conf_users() for pyops.json "users" {}
; pyops.json added "users": {"anonymous": {"debug_port": 5678}} example.

Enqueue-Logic:
enqueue() in lib/runner.py handles debug kind specially
; if kind=="debug", queries existing debug job for owner in running/dequeued states
; kills existing job if found: sends SIGTERM to pid, sets state="cancelled", pid=None, detail="Cancelled by new debug job start", end=datetime.now()
; logs action
; then creates new debug job as todo.

Validation-Logic:
validate_debug_prerequisites(job_id, owner) checks port only
; called in main() after loadJob for kind=="debug"
; fails job to "failed" state with detail if invalid port.

Execution-Logic:
run() injects debugpy code as first lib for debug kind
; compiles debug_bridge.py with debugpy.listen(('127.0.0.1', port)) and wait_for_client()
; keeps listener/glob/logging like draft/service
; exec param/libs/code with debugpy bridge first.

Auto-Install-Debugpy:
Runner injects !debugpy as first lib for debug kind before process_install_lines
; ensures debugpy available like user !pip directives
; processed by same install logic (venv/bin/pip install -q debugpy if not installed).

Tests-Added:
test_api_job.py has debug enqueue tests
; integration tests in tests/integration/runner/ for full debug execution
; test_run_debug_inject asserts debugpy in bridge lib and code compile
; unit tests for validate_debug_prerequisites with port checks
; unit tests for enqueue with existing debug kill.

Global-Attributes:
Debug kind enables VSCode debugger attach to localhost:{port}.
Allows second debug job by killing previous one at enqueue time to handle disconnections.
Overrides allow custom code injection for debugging.

Debug-Overrides:
VSIX DebugService.buildOverrides constructs overrides[`{set}::{name}`] = local fs.readFileSync(fullPath)
; recursive walk pyops/set/*.py basename(relative).py
; runner.run() json.loads(overrides); if f"{set}::{name}" in override_dict: code=override_dict[...]; for lib if lib["filename"] in override_dict: lib["code"]=...
; enables local code in debug jobs matching runner compile(..., f"{set}::{name}.py").

FastAPI-App:
`app/web.py` creates FastAPI application
; mounts routers from `app/routers/`
; serves static files from `app/files/`
; handles dynamic rendering.

Root-Routes:
root() serves root.html
; favicon() serves favicon.ico
; file(path) serves static /files/{path} like ace.js bootstrap.css.

Controller-Routes:
controller(set, name) renders UI via get_controller_code & get_view_content
; loads controller.py globals (set service debug head menu body name)
; injects {{SET}} {{NAME}} in views.
controller_get/set() handles GET /controller/{set}/{name}
; post/put/delete forward to service via ZMQ.
menu() lists controllers from DB.

View-Rendering:
get_controller_code(set, name, debug) reads controller.py
; get_view_content(set, name, debug) reads html views (head menu body).
Dynamic UI uses Bootstrap & Ace & jQuery from /files/
; controllers route requests to /q?cmd= or POST data.

Global-Attributes:
FastAPI uses async routes.
Controllers enable /controller/{set}/{name}/q for API proxy to services.
Views support light/dark theme via Bootstrap data-bs-theme.
Ace Editor loaded dynamically for modes like python json html.

Tests-Structure:
`tests/` uses pytest
; conftest.py provides fixtures mock_conf mock_db mock_client mock_git_dir mock_git_ops etc.
; coverage >90% via pytest --cov-fail-under=90.

Test-Types:
unit/lib/ tests lib_files lib_git lib_pyops lib_runner_utils lib_sets lib_sites.
unit/orm/ tests job schedule.
integration/ tests git orm routers runner execution.
api/ tests api_editor api_endpoints api_job api_schedule api_sets.

Fixtures-Mocks:
mock_db creates temp SQLite.
mock_git_dir creates mock sets/scriptlets.
mock_git_ops overrides list_scriptlets read/write etc.
mock_process mocks subprocess.
mock_croniter mock_jedi mock_datetime.
Overrides for controller_code/view_content file_path etc.

Global-Attributes:
Tests store runtime in `.cache/`.
No autouse fixtures; isolated.
conftest.py custom_showwarning & pytest_configure.
Integration tests prefix routers/ lib/ runner/.

VSIX-Extension:
`vsix/` is VSCodium extension for PyOps
; `src/extension.ts` activates context & registers providers
; `src/jobsTreeProvider.ts` provides JobsTreeDataProvider
; `src/managerTreeProvider.ts` provides ManagerTreeDataProvider
; `src/utils.ts` contains shared functions like inferExt hasValidConfig
; `src/commands/CreateScriptletCommand.ts` handles create scriptlet command logic.

VSIX-Tests:
Unit tests in `tests/` use Jest with mocked vscode APIs & API client
; integration tests in `tests/integration/` use @vscode/test-electron for real VS Code environment with simple assert-based testing
; integration tests run against separately started localhost PyOps development server without authentication
; PyOps server must be started externally before running integration tests (not managed by test framework)
; run unit tests with `npm run test` or `npm run test:coverage`
; run integration tests with `npm run test:integration` (requires running local development PyOps server on localhost:8000)
; integration tests excluded from CI/CD since VS Code not available
; infrastructure set up with simple console-based test runner that works in VS Code extension host
; tests verify extension activation, configuration (server URL only), views, and command registration
; no authentication testing in integration tests (development server runs without auth).

Auth-Service:
`src/services/AuthService.ts` handles auth setup for Basic Auth
; prompts for password if username configured but no password stored
; stores password securely in workspace state
; unit tests in `tests/services/AuthService.test.ts`.

Refresh-Timer-Manager:
`src/services/RefreshTimerManager.ts` manages auto-refresh timers for manager/jobs tree providers
; starts/stops timers based on config validity
; prevents duplicate timers
; unit tests in `tests/services/RefreshTimerManager.test.ts`.

Tree-Providers:
ManagerTreeDataProvider fetches scriptlets via API
; downloads to local .pyops/{set}/
; supports create/upload/save/diff/reset/delete/debug
; has unit tests in `tests/managerTreeProvider.test.ts`.
JobsTreeDataProvider lists jobs by state
; bulk cancel/delete & refresh.

Content-Provider:
RemoteContentProvider serves remote files
; onDidChange events.

Config:
VSCode workspace settings sets serverUrl username password (state) localPyopsDir autoRefreshInterval
; auth optional (Basic if username/password set).

Global-Attributes:
Trees: pyops-manager (sets/scriptlets), pyops-monitor (jobs).
Actions: enqueue debug download view.
Checks hasValidConfig() for serverUrl only.
Status bar shows connection.
Integrates Cline for code gen.
DebugService: `src/services/DebugService.ts` provides buildOverrides (recursive FS walk local pyops/set/*.py) & enqueueDebugJob (API POST /job/item kind=debug)
; used by PyOpsPythonDebugConfigProvider & pyops.startDebugJob
; unit tests `tests/services/debugService.test.ts` >90% coverage.

Extension-Test:
`extension.test.ts` tests activate() success & auth failure
; deactivate() disposals
; config change handler: pyops config only, refresh providers/timers based on hasValidConfig()
; debug terminate: cancel job via API if jobId
; command handlers: 20+ commands via registerCommand capture in beforeAll, mock instances from globals.

Service-Tests:
JobService.test.ts: CRUD ops, bulk cancel/delete, viewJob polling with stdout/stderr updates & state transitions (done/failed/cancelled/remove/404), error handling for all async methods, undefined provider handling, timer cleanup.
; ScriptletService.test.ts: local/remote sync ops, network error handling, filesystem branch tests (existsSync conditions), multi-step error scenarios.
; DebugService.test.ts: buildOverrides, enqueueDebugJob
; DebugOutputMonitor.test.ts: start/stop monitoring & polling (incremental stdout/stderr append, show channels, stop on done/failed/cancelled/remove/404, fetch error log).
; RefreshTimerManager.test.ts: ensureRunning, stopIfRunning
; AuthService.test.ts: setupAuth prompts/storage
; PyOpsPythonDebugConfigProvider.test.ts: config provision.

Provider-Tests:
managerTreeProvider.test.ts: getTreeItem/Children API fetch/download, error handling for fetchScriptlets/downloadScriptlets, refresh graceful failure.
; jobsTreeProvider.test.ts: job states bulk ops
; RemoteContentProvider.test.ts: provideTextDocumentContent, registerRemoteLanguageModeSetter conditional logic, missing language mappings, event emitter access.

Utility-Tests:
utils.test.ts: inferExt all switch cases including unknown types, hasValidConfig false paths (empty/undefined/null serverUrl).

Other-Tests:
apiClient.test.ts: API calls with auth
; ConnectionStatusManager.test.ts: status bar updates
; CreateScriptletCommand.test.ts: command execution.

Test-Mocking:
Hoisted jest.mock('../src/services/*') with mockImplementation for instances/methods
; dynamic require for overrides
; vscode mocks: window.createOutputChannel, workspace.getConfiguration etc.
; global.fetch for API, fs/path mocks for filesystem ops.

Global-Attributes:
Tests use beforeAll for shared activate/setup; beforeEach(jest.clearAllMocks())
; no autouse fixtures; isolation via mocks/clear.
; run: `npm run test --prefix vsix/`
; focus on error paths, edge cases, complex conditional logic for branch coverage.

VSIX-Integration-Monitor:
`vsix/tests/integration/suite/monitor.test.ts` tests JobsTreeDataProvider & JobService
; covers job lifecycle/tree visibility/state description/viewJob(basic)/bulk cancelAllJobs/errors
; uses helpers.pollTree & waitForJobState & createTestJob/Scriptlet
; accesses global.jobsTreeProvider & jobService after activation
; creates print stdout jobs; polls real API; graceful no-crash.
VSIX-Integration-Monitor updates for runner env waits `'done'` state & asserts `'done - task'` description.
; param empty avoids `exec` error.
; test5 `cancelAllJobs` dialog refused in test env.

VSIX-Integration-Manager:
`vsix/tests/integration/suite/manager.test.ts` tests ManagerTreeDataProvider & ScriptletService
; covers full scriptlet lifecycle: create/visibility synced 'check'; download local fs; local edit unsynced 'warning'; reset synced; writeLocalToRemoteDraft synced; saveRemoteDraft commit; delete gone; errors graceful fakeItem.
; uses helpers.pollTreeItemIcon('check'/'warning') editLocalFile pollTree deleteTestScriptlet; accesses global.managerTreeProvider scriptletService.
; polls tree state transitions; verifies local/remote sync via icons; deletes via API helper to avoid dialog in test env.

Runner-Execution-Details:
Runner executes `job.param` as Python code via `exec(compiled_param, glob)`
; retries 3 times on error
; sets state `'failed'` on `NameError` & exec errors
; runs as thread in `web/gunicorn` process.

Build-Process-Insights:
TypeScript compilation requires strict output directory discipline
; compiled JavaScript files must only exist in `out/` directories
; any JS files in source directories indicate misconfiguration.

Integration-Test-Compilation:
Integration tests require separate TypeScript configuration from main extension
; cannot share same tsconfig.json due to different include patterns & output requirements
; rootDir must exactly match directory containing all source files being compiled
; include patterns must explicitly list both test suite files AND utility files.

Output-Directory-Management:
Incorrect rootDir in tsconfig.json leads to nested or misplaced output directories
; outDir path must be calculated relative to rootDir, not tsconfig.json location
; verify compilation output matches expected structure before running tests.

Test-Architecture-Access:
Integration tests in VS Code environment access extension services through global objects
; use `(global as any).serviceName` for service access, not direct TypeScript imports
; static methods accessed via `serviceInstance.constructor.methodName` or class name
; do not assume instance methods exist where only static methods are defined.

VSIX-Integration-Commands:
`vsix/tests/integration/suite/command_integration.test.ts` tests pyops commands execution & effects
; mocks vscode.env.clipboard.writeText (read-only), vscode.window.showWarningMessage (return items[0])
; covers copyJobParam downloadJob deleteJob cancelJob viewJob refreshConnectionStatus openLocalFile diffLocalRemote deleteScriptlet cancelAllJobs deleteAllDone
; asserts tree removal state change no crash
; helpers.pollTree waitForJobState createTestJob deleteTestScriptlet
; accesses global services/providers.

VSIX-ManagerTreeProvider:
ManagerTreeProvider defines interface ScriptletInfo {set: string; name: string; type: string; isLocalOnly?: boolean}
; _scriptlets: ScriptletInfo[]; fetchScriptlets(): Promise<ScriptletInfo[]> /scriptlet/inventory/list
; scanLocalScriptlets(): Promise<ScriptletInfo[]> discovers pyops/{set}/{type}/*.{inferExt(type)} isLocalOnly:true
; refresh merges remote & localOnly; filters excludedSets; downloads remoteOnly sets _syncStatus.

VSIX-LocalOnly-Display:
ManagerTreeProvider.getChildren root: pyopsSet folders; leaf: pyopsItem-{type}(-local)
; localOnly: diff-added icon & contextValue pyopsItem-{type}-local & tooltip &#39;Local only - Set: {set}, Name: {name}, Type: {type}&#39; & description .ext (local)
; remote: check/warning syncStatus icon & contextValue pyopsItem-{type} & tooltip sync status.

VSIX-LocalDebug:
Local-only task scriptlets support pyops.startDebugJob & pyops.stopDebugJob context menus via package.json when /^pyopsItem-task(-local)?$/; sync commands resetLocalFromRemote/saveRemoteDraft/diffLocalRemote restricted excluding -local; writeLocalToRemoteDraft & deleteScriptlet available via /^pyopsItem-(task|service|library|controller|view|markdown)(-local)?$/; writeLocalToRemoteDraft auto-creates remote via PUT /inventory/item if 404 then POST /draft & handles network errors on check/create with specific try-catch showErrorMessages; integration test9 tests write on local-only -> auto-create + draft success.
